thread:
marie (AE): Heads-up — Granite Finance wants a 2‑week POC next week. Primary asks: SSO (SAML), SCIM delta sync, RBAC mapping, and a small Dedicated slot for predictable latency. Quick sync?

ajay (SE): +1. Do we have known SCIM delta throughput constraints for 50k users initial sync then ~200 deltas/hr?

dan (infra): Bulk/import we handle via async job but delta spikes can hit rate limits. Default SCIM rate-limiter is 60 requests/min per org. For 200 deltas/hr that's fine but initial bulk needs our bulk-import workflow.

ajay (SE): Customer specifically said they expect SCIM to push provisioning from Okta in near‑real time. They asked about throttling backfills if we return 429.

anna (security): From Sec side: need domain ownership proof and SAML metadata exchange. Also want a SOC2 copy in the questionnaire. I can send the itemized spreadsheet.

marie (AE): Ok — action items: 1) Confirm SCIM backoff behavior + suggested Okta retry settings, 2) RBAC mapping template (groups -> roles), 3) quote for a tiny Dedicated reservation for POC (1 GPU-ish) and fallback to Hosted.

ajay (SE): For backoff: we return `Retry-After` on 429 and support exponential backoff. Recommended client settings: initial retry 5s, max 120s, jitter. I can paste snippet for their IdP team.

ajay (SE): Snippet:
```
// recommended retry pseudocode
let retry = 5000; // ms
while (attempts < 6) {
  resp = fetch(scim_endpoint, payload);
  if (resp.status == 429) {
    wait(retry + random()*1000);
    retry = Math.min(retry*2, 120000);
    attempts++;
  } else break;
}
```

dan (infra): On RBAC — we have a simple mapping table in Console: group.name -> role.id. For POC, map these three: `admins`, `eng-read`, `billing-read`. We can pre-seed via API.

marie (AE): Can someone draft the mapping template I can send to the prospect? They want example assertions and sample SCIM patch payloads.

ajay (SE): I'll put together a minimal mapping JSON and SCIM Patch example. Also note: if they want username->email canonicalization we recommend casefolding emails before matching.

anna (security): On domain controls, they require multiple domains verified (corp + engineering). We support both via DNS TXT proof; share docs link. Also they asked about SAML assertion encryption — we support signing and optional encryption.

marie (AE): Pricing ask: they want a quote for a 2‑week reserved slot and an option to burst to Hosted if capacity runs out. Any blocker?

dan (infra): We can do a short-term reserved capacity plan (monthly pro‑rata). Pricing note: minimum commit is usually monthly, but we can do a 2‑week credit applied to first month — sales ok?

ajay (SE): For the POC we should enable cache hotkeys for common prompts to keep latency low; that doesn't affect auth but helps the demo.

marie (AE): Great. I'll compile and send a one‑pager to the customer. Ajay + Dan + Anna please drop your artifacts here by EOD: SCIM retry snippet, RBAC mapping JSON, DNS + SAML checklist, and provisional pricing phrasing.

infra-bot: scheduled a follow-up standup reminder in #sales for tomorrow 10:00am. :bell:

ajay (SE): Uploaded RBAC template and SCIM examples to Drive: https://redwood.app/drive/granite-poc (share link, internal).

dan (infra): I'll confirm the pro‑rata quote with finance and paste wording.

anna (security): Sent SOC2 cover page + questionnaire answers draft — PTAL.

marie (AE): Perfect — thanks team. I'll send to Granite and loop them into a tech kickoff. :thumbsup:
